{
  "working": "Evaluate each statement:\n(A) Colloidal particles pass through ordinary filter paper. Typical filter paper pores ~10 µm (10,000 nm), colloids 1–1000 nm, so particles can pass through; statement is generally correct.\n(B) Brownian movement helps keep a sol stable against settling. True; Brownian motion prevents sedimentation.\n(C) Colloidal particles range in size from about 1 nm to 1000 nm. Standard definition: 1 nm to 1 µm (1000 nm); correct.\n(D) True solutions show a strong Tyndall effect. True solutions have molecules small enough that light scattering is negligible; they do not show a strong Tyndall effect. Hence statement D is NOT correct.\nThus the incorrect statement is option D.",
