{
  "working": "Analyze each option:\n(A) Colloidal particles are typically larger than pores in ordinary filter paper, so they pass through; thus statement is false.\n(B) Lyophobic sols are less stable than lyophilic sols because lyophilic particles have better solvation and aggregation; thus false.\n(C) Soap forms micelles only above the critical micelle concentration (CMC); not at any concentration; thus false.\n(D) Soap forms micelles only above the CMC and also above the Krafft temperature (the temperature above which micellization occurs for low-solubility surfactants). This statement correctly describes the condition for micelle formation. Hence (D) is correct.\nThus answer is D.",
