{
  "working": "Analyze each statement.\n(A) Irreversible adiabatic process has q=0 but entropy can increase due to irreversibility; entropy change of system not zero generally. So false.\n(B) Spontaneous process for isolated system increases total entropy; for non-isolated system system entropy may decrease if surroundings increase more. So false.\n(C) In a spontaneous process overall entropy increases; system entropy can decrease if surroundings entropy increase more. This is consistent with second law for non-isolated systems. True.\n(D) Irreversible adiabatic process has q=0 but entropy of system increases because irreversibility generates entropy. True.\nThus correct options are C and D.",
  "answer": "[TYPE: thermodynamics] [CALC_VALUE: CD] [CALC_UNIT: none] [SUBSTANCE: null]",
  "objection": null
}

{
  "working": "Thermodynamic systems classification: open (exchange of both energy and matter), closed (exchange of energy only, no matter), isolated (no exchange of either energy or matter). Evaluate each option:\n(A) Water boiling in an open beaker: matter (steam) leaves, energy (heat) can leave/enter; thus open system. Correct.\n(B) Hot drink in a perfectly insulated, sealed flask: sealed prevents matter exchange; perfectly insulated prevents energy exchange; thus isolated, not open. Incorrect.\n(C) Living cell: exchanges both matter (nutrients, waste) and energy (heat, light); thus open, not closed. Incorrect.\n(D) Gas heated in a sealed rigid steel cylinder: sealed prevents matter exchange; however heating implies energy input from surroundings, so energy exchange occurs; thus not isolated. Incorrect.\nOnly statement (A) is correct.",
  "answer": "[TYPE: thermodynamics] [CALC_VALUE: A] [CALC_UNIT: none] [SUBSTANCE: null]",
  "objection": null
}

{
  "working": "Isolated system: no exchange of energy or matter. A hot drink in a perfectly insulated, sealed flask has no heat exchange (insulated) and no matter exchange (sealed), thus isolated. So (A) correct.\nOpen system: exchanges both energy and matter. A living cell exchanges matter (nutrients, waste) and energy (heat), thus open. So (B) correct.\nClosed system: exchanges energy but not matter. A gas heated in a sealed rigid steel cylinder: sealed prevents matter exchange, cylinder rigid but can allow pressure change; heating provides energy exchange, so closed. So (C) correct.\nClosed system: exchanges energy but not matter. Water boiling in an open beaker: open beaker allows vapor (matter) to leave, thus open, not closed. So (D) incorrect.\nThus correct statements: A, B, C.",
  "answer": "[TYPE: thermodynamics] [CALC_VALUE: ABC] [CALC_UNIT: none] [SUBSTANCE: null]",
